o the point where  it was so it was so hard to win business  then at some point I think I probably in  a moment of weakness quite frankly I was  probably exhausted that's usually how  one learns these lessons because you let  your guard down in a meeting somebody  said we want you to do this this and  that I'm looking at tons of money on the  table and I said I'm really good at that  I'll do that I'm okay at that that I  really strongly recommend you hire  somebody else because I suck at that  I'll work with them but I won't do it  the fact that I said that they wanted to  hire me to do everything even more  because they've never had anybody that  honest all the other sales guys who were  pitching their business for the same  thing told him they were great at  anything and  I was the only one who said so so so the  whole idea of saying I don't know even  to my own colleagues I need help  profoundly profoundly changed the course  of my life turns out we're constantly  surrounded by people who want to help us  including our own clients but they  didn't offer their help but they didn't  think we needed it because we said we  knew everything so for me that lesson  was one of the biggest mistakes that  I've made in my whole career and I think  you when you say was something that went  right was having the courage to ask for  help when I was in really really bad  shape when I was really down to simply  call a friend and say I'm struggling  [Music]  [Music]
 

